\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A bounded remainder}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The integral in \ref{fnip-0092} is the time for the quadratic
model. [Topological equivalence](fnip-0082) keeps the orbits and
loses the dependence on time, as \ref{fnip-0083} records. The
quadratic part on the [center manifold](fnip-0059) still carries a
cubic remainder, so the integral is not the exact time along that
manifold.}

\p{Outside a neighborhood of the fold, the time spent on the closed
curve stays bounded as the current approaches the fold. The quadratic
model supplies the part of the period that grows.
\citet{p. 60}{ermentrout2010mathematical} records that the
frequency becomes arbitrarily low as the current approaches the fold,
and \citet{Exercise 8, p. 72}{ermentrout2010mathematical} asks for
the square-root law.}
